{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/pulls/1","id":4815231081,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVAKx8s8AAAABHwKYaQ","html_url":"https://github.com/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/pull/1.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/issues/1","number":1,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"V1.0.6: unify Win7 WebSocket sessions and repair CMD, terminal and UI lifecycle","user":{"login":"john2000smith7-del","id":245502823,"node_id":"U_kgDODqITZw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245502823?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/john2000smith7-del","html_url":"https://github.com/john2000smith7-del","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/john2000smith7-del/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/john2000smith7-del/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/john2000smith7-del/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/john2000smith7-del/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/john2000smith7-del/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/john2000smith7-del/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/john2000smith7-del/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/john2000smith7-del/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/john2000smith7-del/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"SerialCtl V1.0.5 has separate serial TCP and REST/WS access, redirected CMD stdin corrupts multibyte text and cannot edit a local draft, and primary terminal resizing truncates or fails to reflow output. This change uses one Win7-compatible `serialctl.v1` WebSocket gateway and internal session FIFO, a private native console input bridge with Unicode line editing, and retained logical terminal lines. It also repairs the requested sidebar/power redraw, plus icon, connection scrolling/all-disconnect and modal-owner paths.\n\nOnly existing local serial/CMD sessions and the agreed power query/selected-channel total output actions are exposed. Network connection creation/disconnection, SSH/SFTP and power configuration remain outside the operation whitelist. Pinned PuTTY/YY-Thunks/NI-VISA inputs are unchanged. Native C++17 x64, /MT and PE subsystem 6.01 are preserved.\n\nValidation: [Windows run 38095158673](https://github.com/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/actions/runs/38095158673) **success**, exact source `5f12678e4da327f146edb5ce12eb3b3ea9c8afd0`: clean release.ps1, 14/14 CTest, dependency/Win7/PE checks, ZIP allowlist/reopen/SHA verification, both-theme dynamic desktop captures, real GUI CMD UTF8/GBK/edit/history/paste/follow checks, sustained-output SFTP column drag and all-disconnect, and 10 Python core tests. New full-scrollback reflow and unprinted saved-cursor regressions first failed and now pass; assertions and compatibility checks were retained.\n\n[Portable artifact](https://github.com/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/actions/runs/38095158673/artifacts/11685148611) contains the inner **SerialCtl-V1.0.6-Win7-x64.zip**, **129,982,635 bytes**, SHA-256 **2b27f411489b5b8de432a0e75258c23af149fee7fed7e9cae13d1ce259ae4b54**. Downloaded independently: all 318 members/SHA records checked, including 295 pinned NI-VISA files and byte-identical plink/psftp; MANIFEST source SHA matches this run. [UI evidence](https://github.com/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/actions/runs/38095158673/artifacts/11684839318) contains original desktop/intermediate captures, CTest/build logs and measurement JSON.\n\nMeasured Windows-2022, AMD EPYC 7763 host / 4 logical CPUs, about 16GiB RAM, 1920x1080/96 DPI, loopback, controlled two COM transports: 1/2/8/32-client forwarding P99 0.1022/0.0993/0.1853/0.6928ms. Publish entry to complete client decoding/byte verification; no physical UART time. Actual CMD stdout callback/UI batch to first marker BitBlt P99 light/dark 8.279/8.423ms, 100 samples each, excluding physical display presentation. 35 real CMD sessions were cleared in 0.297s with all recorded descendants exited. Slow-reader isolation verified 9,830,400 healthy bytes. Capacity is 128 idle connections, not a 128-client performance claim; no task-level write lease.\n\nReview mapping and repeatable steps: [V1.0.6 acceptance](docs/testing/V1.0.6-ACCEPTANCE.md), [protocol](docs/architecture/WEBSOCKET-PROTOCOL.md), [Win7/hardware steps](docs/testing/WIN7-HARDWARE-TEST.md), [GUI checklist](docs/testing/MANUAL-REGRESSION.md). The acceptance source file records earlier checkpoints; the final SHA/run/measurements above are the delivery evidence.\n\n**Not run:** actual Win7 SP1/focus/private console bridge, physical UART and IT6332A USB/RS232, real SSH/SFTP server, Linux-to-Win7 wired LAN, 125/150/200% system DPI, Chinese IME composition and 8-hour field stability. Windows-2022, PE inspection and controlled backends do not prove those checks. The original site telnet/FF F4 FF root cause remains unconfirmed. Ctrl+C/full-screen CMD interaction is explicitly unsupported. This draft preserves main/history for independent review.\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T23:38:24Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T23:38:24Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1e92a269c42fd7f4776cedb0df59803f8836cb02","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/pulls/1/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/pulls/1/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/john2000smith7-del/SerialCtl/issues/1/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/john2000smith7-del/Seria